			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@philhawksworth\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>philhawksworth</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@jaredwhite\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jaredwhite</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.xyz/@remotesynth\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>remotesynth</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@brittneypostma\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>brittneypostma</span></a></span> Why does jamstack need saving? Is there some deprecation announcement by some jamstack vendor that I missed?</p>",
